WEBVTT

00:19.450 --> 00:22.280
There are two kinds of heroes.

00:22.280 --> 00:24.590
Heroes who save the world...

00:24.590 --> 00:28.220
and heroes who save single,
nameless individuals.

00:30.530 --> 00:33.260
Well, rumor has it those cretins
from the World Destruction Committee

00:33.260 --> 00:36.600
are hiding out somewhere in town.

00:36.600 --> 00:38.570
So instead of sitting around
here drinking all day long...

00:38.570 --> 00:44.310
how about you try saving the world
by going out and rounding them up?

00:44.310 --> 00:50.070
Unfortunately, I'm the kind of hero
who doesn't save the world, bear-o.

00:59.550 --> 01:02.660
That so-called World Destruction Committee, eh?

01:02.660 --> 01:06.290
People've been sayin' they go around
tearin' things up where they can, but...

01:06.290 --> 01:09.460
Hey, new kid! Stop standin' 'round
like an idiot and take that plate out!

01:09.460 --> 01:10.950
R-Right away!

01:12.800 --> 01:17.440
Hey, what's this? I asked for sand
shark eggs, and this is all I get?!

01:17.440 --> 01:20.010
You know they ain't been catchin'
much lately, so we ain't been gettin' much in.

01:20.010 --> 01:22.010
Now stop yer complainin' and eat!

01:22.010 --> 01:24.570
It's like the end of the world or somethin'!

01:26.950 --> 01:32.510
Well, I guess it doesn't much matter
to me when or where the world ends...

01:35.320 --> 01:38.260
Here's your stewed sand jellyfish, ma'am.

01:38.260 --> 01:40.460
Sorry to keep you waiting.

01:40.460 --> 01:41.600
What's this?

01:41.600 --> 01:43.670
It's the stewed sand jellyfish you ord...

01:43.670 --> 01:45.300
I ordered the whale.

01:45.300 --> 01:46.870
Huh?

01:46.870 --> 01:51.030
What I ordered was sand whale.

01:52.810 --> 01:53.780
A problem?

01:53.780 --> 01:55.780
Uh... no, no problem!

01:55.780 --> 01:56.710
Well, well...

01:56.710 --> 02:01.020
Don't see girls like you
much in a cheap ol' dive like this!

02:01.020 --> 02:03.990
You ain't from around here, are you?

02:03.990 --> 02:05.390
Where'd you come from?

02:05.390 --> 02:07.490
What brings you to our town?

02:07.490 --> 02:10.990
I'm sure you ain't thinking of
trying to get on board the Jifnil,

02:10.990 --> 02:13.060
but if you are, you'd best forget it.

02:13.060 --> 02:17.730
With all the rumors of those World
Destruction Committee yahoos being in town...

02:17.730 --> 02:22.170
- the Jifnil ain't even coming into port.
- Okay, here's your sand whale.
Sorry it took so long!

02:22.170 --> 02:25.370
Anyway, I'm just saying,
after this how 'bout you and me...

02:25.370 --> 02:26.880
I don't think so.

02:26.880 --> 02:29.310
I'd like to eat my food now.

02:29.310 --> 02:31.840
Would you mind leaving me alone?

02:35.150 --> 02:38.140
Everyone freeze! Stay right where you are!

02:39.320 --> 02:42.090
This is the World Salvation Committee.

02:42.090 --> 02:45.420
All we ask is that you sit tight and cooperate.

02:47.730 --> 02:51.330
Hey, we said stay where you are! Are you deaf?!

02:51.330 --> 02:52.770
Freeze! Where are you going?!

02:52.770 --> 02:54.770
So annoying...

02:54.770 --> 02:57.170
I really wish you guys'd just quit it.

02:57.170 --> 03:00.740
Especially when this
lunch cost me everything I had!

03:00.740 --> 03:02.840
Y-You!

03:06.920 --> 03:12.220
I knew it! The World Destruction Committee!

03:14.590 --> 03:16.190
Don't move!

03:16.190 --> 03:19.920
Take one more step and the beastman gets it!

03:21.260 --> 03:22.100
Come with me.

03:22.100 --> 03:25.790
P-Please stop being so rough! You can't...

03:30.970 --> 03:32.600
Fire!

03:50.630 --> 03:53.490
If my eyes are blinded by the sun

03:53.490 --> 03:58.230
I may just see the limits of the light.

03:58.230 --> 04:00.130
The mind of stardust

04:00.130 --> 04:05.970
What a small universe I live in

04:05.970 --> 04:13.510
Won't somebody give me
a code that starts at zero?

04:13.510 --> 04:16.080
Multiplied and in confusion

04:16.080 --> 04:20.120
A colony dead inside its cage

04:20.120 --> 04:24.590
Shoot your cowardly dreams

04:24.590 --> 04:27.760
Loneliness... self-destruct!

04:27.760 --> 04:32.130
No matter what sacrifices we make

04:32.130 --> 04:35.970
for a future just beyond reach

04:35.970 --> 04:39.670
Let our hearts speak to each other

04:39.670 --> 04:42.980
deep down inside

04:42.980 --> 04:47.120
Though the days just one step behind

04:47.120 --> 04:50.120
will pass even farther from us

04:50.120 --> 04:57.180
You will be in my thoughts

05:05.970 --> 05:10.930
"There are Two Kinds of Heroes"

05:26.150 --> 05:28.660
Wait! Wait for me!

05:28.660 --> 05:33.150
Well, it seems the World Destruction
Committee has made an appearance.

05:36.560 --> 05:40.200
What do you want? This is no place for humans.

05:40.200 --> 05:42.270
And especially not for kids such as yourself.

05:42.270 --> 05:46.240
My name is Cain. I've just
come from the Cat Master's manor.

05:46.240 --> 05:50.110
I heard there was a Hero Guild
detective here who helps anyone...

05:50.110 --> 05:53.670
beastmen or humans,
as long as they've got money.

05:57.050 --> 06:00.390
Please help me! Please save my sister!

06:00.390 --> 06:04.850
If you don't save her, she's gonna get
sacrificed to the god of the Sand Sea!

06:09.400 --> 06:11.230
Sire, we just received word

06:11.230 --> 06:14.400
that the World Destruction Committee
has turned up in the town below.

06:14.400 --> 06:18.210
It seems they somehow evaded the forces of the
World Salvation Committee and managed to escape.

06:18.210 --> 06:20.710
You're saying they're still on the run?!

06:20.710 --> 06:24.380
Y-You don't suppose they're on their
way here, to take down the castle?!

06:24.380 --> 06:28.040
Don't worry, sire. Our castle
defenses are impenetrable!

06:28.980 --> 06:33.920
I knew it! Fortune has forsaken this land!
Fishing in the Sand Sea is as bad as ever!

06:33.920 --> 06:36.560
And now the World Salvation Committee!

06:36.560 --> 06:41.060
It's our punishment for neglecting
the god of the Sand Sea for so long!

06:41.060 --> 06:43.660
There's no time to waste!

06:43.660 --> 06:49.400
We have to offer the sacrifice to the
god of the Sand Sea as soon as possible!

06:49.400 --> 06:51.100
Meowessir!

06:58.910 --> 07:03.420
So what's your deal? Why would
a human work at a beastman café?

07:03.420 --> 07:05.850
And on top of that you almost
got us turned into swiss cheese!

07:05.850 --> 07:07.190
You're one to talk!

07:07.190 --> 07:11.630
I'd just managed to fool the beastmen
and get myself hired on with room and board.

07:11.630 --> 07:15.800
Wait, so you infiltrated that café in
order to carry out some kind of plot?

07:15.800 --> 07:17.700
Nah, I just needed the job.

07:17.700 --> 07:21.870
You gotta work to make a living, you know.

07:21.870 --> 07:24.670
And they pay better at beastman establishments.

07:24.670 --> 07:26.710
Just for a stupid job?!

07:26.710 --> 07:30.110
There's no telling what they'd do to
you if they found out you're human!

07:30.110 --> 07:34.380
Looks like you took care
of that one for me... Morte.

07:35.980 --> 07:39.120
How do you know my name?

07:39.120 --> 07:41.960
Well, it was written right
there on your wanted poster...

07:41.960 --> 07:44.560
"World Destruction Committee
member Morte Urshela, age 17..."

07:44.560 --> 07:45.890
I'm 16!

07:45.890 --> 07:47.660
There's a big difference
between 16 and 17!

07:47.660 --> 07:52.070
- Her age? She's worried about her age?
And not that they know her name?!
- Every year in your teens is precious!

07:52.070 --> 07:54.470
You're human, so you should know better

07:54.470 --> 07:56.970
than to just believe everything
the World Salvation Committee says!

07:56.970 --> 07:59.130
I can't believe what an idiot you are!

07:59.670 --> 08:00.510
But anyway, you're...

08:00.510 --> 08:01.980
Kyrie!

08:01.980 --> 08:03.410
My name is Kyrie Illnis.

08:03.410 --> 08:06.350
I wasn't actually asking your name.

08:06.350 --> 08:09.080
So, what is the World
Destruction Committee, anyway?

08:09.080 --> 08:10.990
How should I know?

08:10.990 --> 08:14.820
Those jerks just stuck the label
on me and started chasing me around.

08:14.820 --> 08:17.360
By "those jerks," you mean
the World Salvation Committee?

08:17.360 --> 08:18.230
Yep.

08:18.230 --> 08:22.230
But at this point, I'm actually
glad they gave me such a cool name.

08:22.230 --> 08:26.720
It packs a punch, don't you think?
The "World Destruction Committee"!

08:38.750 --> 08:40.580
Uh... hi...

08:40.580 --> 08:42.880
Who are you guys?

08:42.880 --> 08:49.020
Um... we're just, uh...
wanderers passing through?

08:49.420 --> 08:52.560
Have you seen a boy named Cain?

08:52.560 --> 08:54.460
He's my little brother.

08:54.460 --> 08:56.360
Sorry, but we haven't seen him.

08:56.360 --> 08:58.730
Linan!

08:58.730 --> 09:00.970
Linan, what are you doing?

09:00.970 --> 09:06.240
Oh, Elder. I can't find Cain,
so I've been looking for him.

09:06.240 --> 09:09.610
Who are these two? I haven't
seen them around the village.

09:09.610 --> 09:11.700
They said they're wanderers.

09:12.950 --> 09:14.450
You're travelers?

09:14.450 --> 09:18.890
At your service. Trust me,
there's nothing suspicious about us!

09:20.760 --> 09:25.950
Well, the sun's going down.
Why don't you stay the night in our village?

09:37.840 --> 09:44.180
Mm, that was good! But I feel
kinda tired now that my belly's full.

09:46.450 --> 09:49.280
You're not gonna finish yours?

09:49.280 --> 09:52.740
In that case, I'll go ahead and
take this sand jellyfish stew here...

09:58.760 --> 10:01.330
So, what are you going to do after this?

10:01.330 --> 10:02.830
What can I do?

10:02.830 --> 10:06.670
The café's in shambles and
they know I'm human now.

10:06.670 --> 10:09.300
Plus, I don't have any
place to go home to anyway.

10:09.300 --> 10:11.870
Say, are you gonna eat
that soy-glazed jellyfish?

10:11.870 --> 10:13.710
I hate sand jellyfish.

10:13.710 --> 10:15.370
All right, I'll eat it.

10:16.210 --> 10:21.620
Hey, I know! I'll ask the
village elder if I can stay here.

10:21.620 --> 10:23.780
The people seem nice enough.

10:23.780 --> 10:25.720
Why don't you do the same?

10:27.990 --> 10:31.060
As soon as I've rested, I'm leaving.

10:31.060 --> 10:33.560
Leaving? Where to?

10:33.560 --> 10:36.830
To destroy the world.

10:36.830 --> 10:38.570
Are you serious?

10:38.570 --> 10:40.200
Of course.

10:40.200 --> 10:43.070
But if you destroy the world,
it won't be just the beastmen who die off.

10:43.070 --> 10:44.670
Humans will die off too.

10:44.670 --> 10:47.540
Beastmen, humans... who cares.

10:47.540 --> 10:52.150
All I'm interested in is smashing
this ridiculous world to pieces.

10:52.150 --> 10:54.680
Don't you think you should
rethink your plan a little?

10:54.680 --> 10:57.650
I mean, you can't really
destroy the world on your own.

10:57.650 --> 11:02.360
And besides, the whole idea of "world
destruction" is pretty vague to begin with.

11:02.360 --> 11:05.260
With this, all it takes is one person.

11:14.270 --> 11:14.940
What is that?

11:14.940 --> 11:16.340
Don't touch it!

11:16.340 --> 11:19.740
This has the power to destroy the
entire world in the blink of an eye!

11:19.740 --> 11:22.080
It's called the Destruct Code.

11:22.080 --> 11:26.780
It hides secrets that
humans can't possibly understand.

11:26.780 --> 11:31.920
That's why it's probably best for
you if you don't get involved with me.

11:31.920 --> 11:38.130
You should just put on those fake
ears and quietly wait it out in some café

11:38.130 --> 11:40.430
until the end of the world comes.

11:40.430 --> 11:43.960
Because I'll be the one to end it.

11:43.960 --> 11:45.860
And I won't let anyone stand in my...!

11:55.210 --> 11:58.210
So we use that girl in place of Linan?

11:58.210 --> 12:03.240
Yes. No one'll notice if
some traveler goes missing.

12:04.420 --> 12:06.920
But Elder, wait!

12:06.920 --> 12:08.820
What is it, Linan?

12:08.820 --> 12:12.590
It's just... sacrificing a
total stranger in my place...

12:12.590 --> 12:14.430
It's nothing for you to be concerned about.

12:14.430 --> 12:16.730
She's just a traveler with no family.

12:16.730 --> 12:18.800
No one'll be sad if she dies.

12:18.800 --> 12:22.000
And in exchange, you will be saved.

13:02.610 --> 13:05.350
Where is the girl for the sacrifice?

13:05.350 --> 13:07.980
We are preparing her as we speak, sire.

13:07.980 --> 13:10.310
I beg your patience.

13:13.620 --> 13:15.150
That the place, bear-o?

13:34.070 --> 13:34.740
She ran away?!

13:34.740 --> 13:37.550
She didn't eat the sand jellyfish?

13:37.550 --> 13:38.850
What are we gonna do?!

13:38.850 --> 13:40.710
Don't ask me!

14:04.210 --> 14:06.570
Don't move!

14:06.570 --> 14:08.740
Oh, it's you.

14:08.740 --> 14:11.210
I'm sorry I left without saying thanks.

14:11.210 --> 14:15.280
It's not that I didn't trust you. It's just
that I've been through a lot, and well...

14:15.280 --> 14:16.250
If you're looking for the guy I left back...

14:16.250 --> 14:17.920
That's not it!

14:17.920 --> 14:19.550
Something terrible's about to happen!

14:19.550 --> 14:25.290
The other wanderer... they took
him instead of me. He's gonna be a...

14:25.290 --> 14:27.120
a human sacrifice!

14:44.710 --> 14:55.120
Meowgolus meowgolus meow meow meow!
Meowgolus meowgolus meow meow meow!

14:55.120 --> 14:59.230
Woaa... meowun!

14:59.230 --> 15:01.250
Meowun!

15:07.740 --> 15:10.270
Meowun!

15:10.270 --> 15:12.240
Runny jellyfish...

15:31.360 --> 15:32.590
Beh?!

15:33.530 --> 15:36.960
Wh-Who the hellcat are you?!

15:36.960 --> 15:39.690
I'm the World Destruction Committee!

15:44.670 --> 15:48.610
You! How dare you interfere
with our human sacrifice ceremony!

15:48.610 --> 15:52.550
Knock it off with all that corny
nonsense and tell me where he is!

15:52.550 --> 15:54.950
Where is Kyrie?

15:54.950 --> 15:58.050
Which one of you bozos said
our defenses were impenetrable?!

15:58.050 --> 15:59.790
You worthless...

15:59.790 --> 16:02.860
If you don't tell me where Kyrie is,
I'll take this one instead...

16:02.860 --> 16:06.190
and make him your sacrifice!

16:06.190 --> 16:07.720
Oh, I guess he's down there.

16:18.010 --> 16:20.370
Be-Be-Behind you!

16:20.370 --> 16:22.570
It's a man?!

16:31.490 --> 16:33.540
Kyrie!

16:33.990 --> 16:35.480
Morte!

16:38.990 --> 16:40.390
Stand up!

16:47.570 --> 16:50.500
We found you!
And this time you're not getting away!

16:57.340 --> 17:01.280
I swear... things always get
complicated at the worst times!

17:04.920 --> 17:07.390
Stay right here, bear-o!

17:09.290 --> 17:10.380
Cain!

17:11.790 --> 17:13.050
Sis!

17:18.770 --> 17:20.390
Cease fire!

17:28.380 --> 17:31.550
Wh-What are you doing? Cut my ropes first!

17:31.550 --> 17:34.210
Just sit tight while I mop up these goons.

17:34.210 --> 17:35.980
Are you kidding me?!

18:15.460 --> 18:17.260
That's enough!

18:17.260 --> 18:19.160
Drop the blade!

18:25.200 --> 18:28.330
This is why I told you to cut my ropes first...

18:50.120 --> 18:52.680
No, not again!

18:57.660 --> 18:59.330
Linan!

19:08.680 --> 19:12.200
Are you hurt, little gir... bear-o?!

19:12.980 --> 19:16.350
You little...! Are you a member of the
World Destruction Committee too?!

19:16.350 --> 19:17.320
No, I just, uh...

19:17.320 --> 19:19.520
Just kill him along with the others!

19:19.520 --> 19:21.080
But I'm not with them!

19:22.520 --> 19:25.230
That's far enough!

19:25.230 --> 19:28.660
Or else I'll activate this.

19:28.660 --> 19:31.320
Th-The Destruct Code?!

19:33.830 --> 19:35.170
It's a bluff!

19:35.170 --> 19:37.930
If you've got what it takes,
then go ahead and do it!

19:40.770 --> 19:42.710
You're bluffing?!

19:43.410 --> 19:45.780
Now be a good girl and hand it over!

19:58.090 --> 20:00.060
Wh-What's going on?

20:07.130 --> 20:08.570
Bring it!

20:12.140 --> 20:13.240
You can't be serious!

20:13.240 --> 20:15.440
Get the lead out, bear-o!

20:28.060 --> 20:32.660
Will the world really be
annihilated if you use this?

20:32.660 --> 20:35.490
Yeah, if you know how to use it right.

20:36.730 --> 20:40.300
But that was the first time
I've ever seen it glow like that.

20:40.300 --> 20:41.840
Did you do something to it?

20:41.840 --> 20:45.170
What?! I didn't do anything!

20:45.170 --> 20:48.800
Okay, whatever. Just give it back.

20:54.410 --> 20:56.980
Hey, thank you guys so much.

20:56.980 --> 20:59.450
We're the World Destruction Committee.

20:59.450 --> 21:03.920
- "We"?
- We haven't done
anything to deserve your thanks.

21:03.920 --> 21:06.260
Mr. Detective...

21:11.770 --> 21:13.130
Well, see you later!

21:13.130 --> 21:15.940
Hey, where're you going?!

21:15.940 --> 21:18.940
I'm taking this boat.

21:18.940 --> 21:23.600
So those two were from the
World Destruction Committee...

21:29.020 --> 21:30.950
Yo, bear-o!

21:32.350 --> 21:34.490
You filthy boat thief, bear-o!

21:34.490 --> 21:36.320
Who the heck is that bear?

21:36.320 --> 21:41.700
I, uh... think he's a
detective from the Hero Guild.

21:41.700 --> 21:43.360
Get off!

21:43.360 --> 21:44.670
I think I should just point out

21:44.670 --> 21:48.900
that they also thought you were a
member of the World Destruction Committee.

21:48.900 --> 21:51.000
Which means you just escaped with us.

21:51.000 --> 21:52.240
Well, bear...

21:52.240 --> 21:53.340
that's a tough break.

21:53.340 --> 21:55.070
That goes for you too.

21:58.710 --> 22:01.210
So what do we do now?

22:01.210 --> 22:03.480
I already told you.

22:03.480 --> 22:06.420
We're going to destroy the world.

22:08.090 --> 22:11.760
It turns out there's another kind of hero.

22:11.760 --> 22:17.030
The kind of hero who leads
the world to destruction... bear-o.

22:21.230 --> 22:24.740
The glimmering seas of sand

22:24.740 --> 22:27.870
The end of the green earth

22:27.870 --> 22:33.950
Memories overflowing from the sky

22:33.950 --> 22:37.080
now plunged into darkness

22:37.080 --> 22:40.290
The memories will pile up

22:40.290 --> 22:46.290
like mounds of rubble

22:46.290 --> 22:49.530
Mutual encounters

22:49.530 --> 22:52.600
Misunderstood feelings

22:52.600 --> 22:55.740
Interwoven words

22:55.740 --> 22:58.870
People hurting each other

22:58.870 --> 23:10.980
Does the path we walk on
still lead us to tomorrow?

23:13.820 --> 23:17.660
Living this moment against the world

23:17.660 --> 23:20.660
isn't just about changing the world

23:20.660 --> 23:26.230
We're off on a distant journey across the waves

23:26.230 --> 23:29.800
So let our living heartbeat echo in the wind

23:29.800 --> 23:33.340
Around the world, to the end of the world

23:33.340 --> 23:39.310
Until we reach

23:39.310 --> 23:50.920
the promised land just beyond

23:53.430 --> 23:58.370
After giving the slip to our annoying pursuers,
we found ourselves on the pleasure ship Jifnil.

23:58.370 --> 24:00.470
In this maelstrom of hopes and dreams,

24:00.470 --> 24:05.040
we meet a smuggler and two people
from the World Salvation Committee.

24:05.040 --> 24:07.810
But wait... a card game with
the Destruct Code on the line?!

24:07.810 --> 24:10.710
Fine by me! Bring it on!

24:10.710 --> 24:13.350
Next time on World Destruction... Episode 2:

24:13.350 --> 24:15.850
"There Are Two Kinds of Worlds."

24:15.850 --> 24:18.350
So how come the two of us
hafta be on the wanted list too?

24:18.350 --> 24:19.510
Bear-o.
